#: ../../how-to/protect-data-access.md:1
msgid "Protect access to your data"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/protect-data-access.md:3
msgid ""
"Cadrumo encrypts every profile, transaction, piece of evidence, and "
"filing under one master key. Your passphrase opens that key. If you lose "
"the passphrase and have no recovery key, the data cannot be decrypted by "
"anyone, including you."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/protect-data-access.md:8
msgid ""
"Use this guide to set up a recovery key before you need it, change your "
"passphrase, recover access after a lost passphrase, log out safely, and "
"reset local state only as a last resort."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/protect-data-access.md:12
msgid "Before you start"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/protect-data-access.md:14
msgid "You need:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/protect-data-access.md:16
msgid ""
"An active profile - see [set up your taxpayer profile](profile-setup.md)."
" The first command below refuses without one (`No se pudo determinar "
"ningún bucket activo. Selecciona un perfil y vuelve a intentarlo.`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/protect-data-access.md:19
msgid ""
"Your current master-key passphrase for recovery-key creation, rotation, "
"and passphrase changes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/protect-data-access.md:21
msgid ""
"Your recovery words for verification or recovery after a lost passphrase."
" Recovery sets a new passphrase without requiring the lost one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/protect-data-access.md:24
msgid ""
"Use `--language en`, `es`, `ca`, or `hu` when you need a specific output "
"language."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/protect-data-access.md:27
msgid "Create your recovery key first"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/protect-data-access.md:29
msgid "Do this once, right after setup, while your passphrase still works:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/protect-data-access.md:34
msgid ""
"If no recovery key exists yet, the command creates one and prints a "
"twenty-four-word recovery key. The words are shown exactly once and are "
"never stored. Only an encrypted wrapper of the master key is written to "
"disk. Write the words down and keep them offline, separate from your "
"computer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/protect-data-access.md:39
msgid ""
"Run the same command again later to confirm enrollment: once a recovery "
"key exists, the command reports its status and does not print the words "
"again."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/protect-data-access.md:42
msgid "Check that your recovery key works"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/protect-data-access.md:44
msgid "Verify the words you wrote down without changing anything:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/protect-data-access.md:49
msgid ""
"The command reports `verified yes` or `verified no` and exits with a "
"failure code when the words do not open the recovery wrapper. Nothing is "
"modified either way."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/protect-data-access.md:53
msgid "Replace the recovery key"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/protect-data-access.md:55
msgid ""
"If the written words may have been seen by someone else, mint a fresh "
"recovery key:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/protect-data-access.md:61
msgid ""
"New words are printed exactly once. The previous recovery words stop "
"working immediately. Store the new words as before."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/protect-data-access.md:64
msgid "Change your passphrase"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/protect-data-access.md:66
msgid "To change the passphrase while you still know the current one:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/protect-data-access.md:71
msgid ""
"The command asks for the current passphrase if the store is not already "
"open, then prompts twice (hidden) for the new one. The master key itself "
"does not change, so all stored data stays readable. Only the passphrase "
"that opens it is replaced. For non-interactive use, pass `--new-"
"passphrase` together with `--confirm-new-passphrase`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/protect-data-access.md:77
msgid "Recover after a forgotten passphrase"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/protect-data-access.md:79
msgid "If you forgot the passphrase but have your recovery words:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/protect-data-access.md:84
msgid ""
"The command prompts twice (hidden) for a new passphrase, unlocks the "
"master key from the recovery wrapper, and rewraps it under the new "
"passphrase. All stored data stays intact. Nothing is deleted or re-"
"encrypted. For non-interactive use, pass `--new-passphrase` together with"
" `--confirm-new-passphrase` instead of being prompted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/protect-data-access.md:90
msgid ""
"If you have neither the passphrase nor the recovery words, the encrypted "
"data is permanently unreadable. The only way forward is a reset (below), "
"which deletes it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/protect-data-access.md:94
msgid "Run without a passphrase prompt"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/protect-data-access.md:96
msgid ""
"Automation cannot answer an interactive passphrase prompt. For an agent "
"server, scheduled job, or script, set `CADRUMO_SECRET_PASSPHRASE` for "
"that process. Treat the value like the passphrase itself. Never put it in"
" a shared shell profile, committed script, or log."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/protect-data-access.md:101
msgid ""
"Interactive commands prompt when they need the current passphrase. "
"Recovery commands use the recovery words and ask for a new passphrase "
"instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/protect-data-access.md:104
msgid "Log out of the active profile"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/protect-data-access.md:106
msgid ""
"Use `aeat config profile logout` when you finish working with a profile. "
"Logout closes the active storage session, discards in-memory key "
"material, disposes the bucket engines, and clears the active-profile "
"selection:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/protect-data-access.md:114
msgid ""
"Nothing in the profile is deleted. Select it again with `aeat config "
"switch <name>` when you return."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/protect-data-access.md:117
msgid "Reset local state (last resort)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/protect-data-access.md:119
msgid ""
"Export every profile you want to keep before continuing. Reset "
"permanently deletes every profile stored locally, related local "
"authentication state, and the active profile selection. It doesn't delete"
" exports stored elsewhere. You can't undo the reset."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/protect-data-access.md:127
msgid ""
"Use `start` only when you intend to remove all local profiles. Confirm "
"the reset explicitly. It checks retention requirements before deleting "
"anything and refuses to start while another reset is incomplete."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/protect-data-access.md:130
msgid ""
"Use the read-only `status` command to inspect the latest operation "
"without changing local data. Provide an operation ID to inspect an exact "
"operation. Status reports an incomplete, paused, or complete operation. "
"Its output includes the operation ID and any pause reason."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/protect-data-access.md:134
msgid ""
"Use `resume` after an interruption or pause. Confirm the reset again. It "
"continues the same incomplete operation instead of creating another. "
"Provide an operation ID to resume an exact operation. After deletion "
"starts, resuming the reset doesn't restore deleted data."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/protect-data-access.md:139
msgid ""
"If legal retention requirements pause the reset, stop if you must keep "
"the affected records. Override the pause only after reviewing and "
"accepting the legal retention consequence, and always provide a non-empty"
" reason. If you provide a reason without the override, the command "
"refuses to continue."
msgstr ""

